{% doc %}
  Pagination for `<swiper-carousel>`: dots, a slide counter, or a progress bar.

  ## Dots are markup, the other two are computed

  Dots use `data-ref="indicators"` and `data-indicator`, which `SwiperCarousel`
  already owns — it wires the clicks, tracks the current one and hides the whole
  group when the track does not scroll. Nothing new is needed for them.

  Numbers and the progress bar cannot be Liquid, because Liquid does not know
  how many slides fit in the viewport and therefore cannot know how many pages
  there are. `<carousel-pagination>` computes that at runtime from the parent
  carousel.

  It is a sibling component rather than a change to `SwiperCarousel` so that
  the carousel keeps working untouched when pagination is set to None, which is
  the default and by far the common case.

  Parameters:
    style    (string, required)  'dots' | 'numbers' | 'progress'
    settings (object)

  @example
    {% render 'carousel-pagination', style: 'dots', settings: section.settings %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign style = style | default: 'none'
-%}

{%- case style -%}
  {%- when 'dots' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      One dot per slide. The component hides any that turn out to be
      unreachable once it has measured the track, so an over-count here is
      corrected rather than left dangling.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="carousel-shell__dots" data-ref="indicators">
      {%- for i in (1..slide_count) -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="carousel-shell__dot"
          data-indicator
          aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.go_to_slide' | t: index: forloop.index }}"
        ></button>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

  {%- when 'numbers' -%}
    <carousel-pagination class="carousel-shell__counter" data-style="numbers">
      <span class="carousel-shell__counter-current" data-ref="current">1</span>
      <span class="carousel-shell__counter-separator" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="carousel-shell__counter-total" data-ref="total">1</span>
    </carousel-pagination>

  {%- when 'progress' -%}
    <carousel-pagination class="carousel-shell__progress" data-style="progress">
      {%- comment -%}
        Presentational only. The slide position is already announced through the
        carousel's `role="status"` region, and a second announcement of the same
        change is noise, not redundancy.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="carousel-shell__progress-bar" data-ref="bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </carousel-pagination>
{%- endcase -%}
